    "result_text": "The build is green. All tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds a computed `displayName` field to the owner API response, formatted as `LastName, FirstName` from the stored names.\n\n**What I did:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` response schema. Since the DTOs (`OwnerDto`) are generated from this spec at build time, this gives the response a `displayName` field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct mapping that populates `displayName` from the `Owner` entity via a new `toDisplayName` helper returning `lastName + \", \" + firstName` (null-safe).\n\nThe flow: `POST /api/owners` creates the owner, `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns it through `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(...)`, which now emits `displayName`. The acceptance test `coreComputesDisplayName` (asserting `$.displayName == \"<LastName>, John\"`) passes, and the full suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).",
